# AGENTS.md — Binding rules for agentic development

> This file is the **operational contract** for any AI agent (Claude, Gemini, Copilot, Cursor, Codex, ...) that writes, modifies, or reviews code in this repository.
>
> **Before any task**, read, in order:
>
> 1. This file (`AGENTS.md`)
> 2. [`docs/INDEX.md`](docs/INDEX.md)
> 3. [`docs/architecture/ARCHITECTURE_OVERVIEW.md`](docs/architecture/ARCHITECTURE_OVERVIEW.md) — technical Single Source of Truth
> 4. The current milestone block in [`docs/planning/ROADMAP_MILESTONES.md`](docs/planning/ROADMAP_MILESTONES.md)
> 5. Any task brief under `docs/tasks/` (if present)

## 0. Project identity

- **Repo**: `${REPO_SLUG}` — ${PROJECT_KIND}.
- **Single Source of Truth (SSoT)**: ${SSOT_NAME}. This repo consumes truth from there and never duplicates it.
- **Audience**: ${PRIMARY_AUDIENCE}.
- **Non-audience**: ${NON_AUDIENCE}.

## 1. Non-negotiable principles

1. **SSoT external.** This repo does not duplicate domain logic, does not implement "smart" fallbacks, does not compute authorization itself. Anything that decides domain state flows from the SSoT.
2. **No direct access to underlying data stores, message brokers, object storage, or secrets.** Only through the SSoT's authorized boundary.
3. **Authorization is server-side; UI is cosmetic.** The SSoT decides. The client hides/disables but never grants.
4. **Audit is mandatory for sensitive actions.** A feature without audit trail is not a feature.
5. **Schema-driven, never stringly-typed.** Every payload at a boundary is validated. No `any` at the boundary.
6. **Idempotent mutations.** Every state-changing call carries an `Idempotency-Key` (UUID v4).
7. **Long-running work is observable.** Operations that exceed UX-acceptable latency become a first-class `Job`, polled or streamed, never blocking the UI.
8. **UTC for time, normalized format for geo** (where applicable). Persist in canonical form; render in the user's locale.
9. **No secrets in the client.** Tokens/keys are reveal-once, then last-four only. Never in `localStorage` or equivalents long-term.
10. **Forward-compatible schemas.** Every response carries a schema version header; tolerate unknown fields; never fail on additive changes.

## 2. Scope of this repository

**IN scope:**

- ${PROJECT_KIND}-specific code (UI / pages / routes / state / forms / ...).
- Typed boundary client (HTTP / IPC / SDK wrapper) with schema validation.
- Tests (unit / integration / E2E) for everything above.
- Optional thin edge layer (BFF / proxy) for cross-cutting concerns (CSRF, session, CSP).

**OUT of scope:**

- Domain models / migrations / scheduler / workers (live in the SSoT solution).
- Policy / configuration definitions (live in the SSoT; this repo only edits them via authorized endpoints).
- Direct database / queue / storage access.

If a task requires changes *outside* this scope, the agent produces a **proposal** in `docs/architecture/proposals/` and stops. It does not simulate the missing piece client-side.

## 3. Agentic workflow (standard)

For any non-trivial task:

1. **Plan** — 3–7 step plan in chat (or in `docs/tasks/<id>.md`) before touching code.
2. **Read context** — milestone, related schemas, existing components. No duplication.
3. **Schema first** — when a boundary changes, update validators (and derived types) before call sites.
4. **Implement** — small files, business logic in hooks/services, no inline boundary calls inside UI components.
5. **Test** — at least one unit/integration test per new hook/service; smoke E2E for new pages.
6. **Verify** — `typecheck`, `lint`, `test`, `build` all green.
7. **Document** — update Execution Spec slice, FR coverage, INDEX, ADR (if architectural). Same PR.

## 4. Code conventions

- **Language / runtime**: see [`docs/architecture/TECH_STACK.md`](docs/architecture/TECH_STACK.md).
- **Naming**: PascalCase types/components, camelCase functions/variables, SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE constants, kebab-case route files.
- **Folder structure**: see Tech Stack — binding.
- **Soft cap**: ~200 lines per file.
- **No `console.log` in committed code** (use the shared logger).
- **No `// @ts-ignore`** (or equivalent) without `// reason:` comment.

## 5. Security baseline

See [`docs/architecture/SECURITY_AND_AUTH.md`](docs/architecture/SECURITY_AND_AUTH.md). Highlights:

- Tokens in memory or httpOnly cookie. Never `localStorage` long-lived.
- CSRF via double-submit token if cookie-based auth.
- No `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` (or equivalent) without sanitization + comment.
- CSP rigorous; no inline scripts.
- All input validated client-side; the SSoT is still the last authority.
- Signed URLs for any large file download.

## 6. Interaction with the SSoT

- **One typed client** for the SSoT. No ad-hoc `fetch` / `axios` calls in feature code.
- Conventions: see [`docs/architecture/INTEGRATION_CONTRACT.md`](docs/architecture/INTEGRATION_CONTRACT.md).
- Missing endpoint → open issue / proposal. Do not improvise client-side.

## 7. UI/state conventions (if applicable)

- **Server state**: managed via the canonical server-state library (see Tech Stack).
- **UI state**: local hooks; minimal global store.
- **Form state**: schema-driven form library; client-side validation mirrors SSoT validation.
- **Routing**: declarative; permissions checked via a loader / guard component.

## 8. UI/UX rules (if applicable)

If this project uses a UI flavor, read its `docs/ui-ux/DESIGN_PRINCIPLES.md`. Highlights:

- Destructive confirmations require typing the resource name.
- Long-running operations show as `Job` with a link to detail.
- A11y WCAG 2.1 AA minimum.
- i18n strings from the dictionary; no concatenation.
- Dark mode supported from day-1 (if UI project).

## 9. The agent must NEVER

- Create endpoints / migrations / ETL / ingest workers — those live in the SSoT.
- Bypass the typed boundary client.
- Reimplement authorization rules client-side beyond cosmetic hide/disable.
- Add a heavyweight dependency (>100 KB gzipped) without a written ADR justification.
- Introduce an alternative framework alongside the chosen one without ADR.
- Insert mock data instead of real endpoints in production code (mocks live only in tests and dev MSW).
- Create new documentation files unless asked — update existing docs instead.
- Touch files under `docs/guidelines/` (read-only input from external owners).

## 10. Definition of Done (per PR)

- [ ] `typecheck`, `lint`, `test`, `build` green
- [ ] New boundary code has schema + at least one test
- [ ] New user-facing routes have a smoke E2E
- [ ] Execution Spec slice tracker updated
- [ ] FR coverage updated in `FUNCTIONAL_REQUIREMENTS.md`
- [ ] Milestone DoD box ticked if applicable
- [ ] ADR opened if architectural decision was made
- [ ] No regression in a11y on touched UI pages
- [ ] No secrets / hard-coded URLs
- [ ] Audit / confirmations present for sensitive actions

